From 43d3a6f001054224349ff18f23b4eba8421d19ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhai patchset migration <erhai-patchset@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:13:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: reserve ADSP heap outside reusable
 CMA

The 7.3 FastRPC driver assigns the complete ADSP remote heap to DSP VMIDs during probe. A reusable CMA pool can still back unrelated anonymous Linux pages after the CPU loses access to that memory. Native kernel compilation on Erhai produced synchronous external aborts in clear_page for six huge-page allocations inside the 12 MiB heap at fec00000-ff7fffff.

Keep the dynamically allocated below-4G heap dedicated and unmapped instead of reusable. This matches its channel-lifetime ownership and prevents ordinary Linux allocations from receiving DSP-owned pages.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index a9a4fc2d3..8b3fbc5cd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -595,7 +595,8 @@ adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem: adsp-rpc-remote-heap {
 			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x00000000 0x0 0xffffffff>;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
 			size = <0x0 0xc00000>;
-			reusable;
+			/* FastRPC assigns the whole heap to DSP VMIDs at probe. */
+			no-map;
 		};
 	};
 
